<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=wind-turbine">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wind turbine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A wind turbine is a device that converts the kinetic energy of wind into electrical energy. The first to generate electricity was installed by the Austrian Josef Friedländer at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> International Electrical Exhibition in 1883: a Halladay wind motor 6.6 m across, whose 3.7 kW drove a dynamo that charged batteries. James Blyth lit his holiday home in Marykirk, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, with one in July 1887, and Charles F. Brush built the first automatically operated wind turbine some months later. A 100 kW forerunner of modern horizontal-axis machines ran at Yalta in 1931, and by 2024 turbines generated over 1,136 gigawatts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wind-turbine.jpg" alt="Wind turbine" width="330" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniela Kloth · GFDL 1.2 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019_07_26_Trampe_Windkraftanlagen_DJI_0041.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1883</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Vienna</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Josef Friedländer</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Wind had powered machines since the windwheel of Hero of Alexandria and the vertical-axle windmills built in Sistan from the 7th century; Friedländer's machine of 1883 was the first to generate electricity.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/windmill">Windmill<span>9th century</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/voltaic-pile">Electric battery<span>1800</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/electric-generator">Electric generator<span>1831</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=wind-turbine">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
